// src/kernel/boot/witness/pdxfs_first_mount.pdx -- R53.M4-003 (#1750)
//
// FIRST MOUNT terminal witness for the R53.M4 --with-disk smoke.
// Emits a single ordered "FIRST MOUNT OK" fingerprint at the terminal
// position of the boot-mode PDXB volume-lifecycle sequence, closing the
// R53.M4-003 (`boot_r53_first_mount`) smoke against a QEMU-attached
// blank NVMe device that sibling R53.M4-001 (#1748) --with-disk flag
// parsing and R53.M4-002 (#1749) image-lifecycle wiring attach.
//
// =============================================================================
// WHERE THIS FITS IN THE R53.M4 FIRST-MOUNT SEQUENCE
// =============================================================================
//
// The first-mount smoke exercises the PDXB volume-lifecycle path end to
// end on a live disk. Under `run-smoke.sh --with-disk boot_r53_first_
// mount` (design/tooling/volume-lifecycle-mechanism.md §7.3), the smoke
// runner attaches a mkfs'd 128 MiB raw image as an emulated NVMe
// namespace, and the golden (tests/r53/first-mount.golden) pins the
// five ordered fingerprints the LIVE arm of the boot chain produces:
//
//   (1) PDXB PROBE OK          probe.pdx (#1706) validates LBA 0 and
//                              registers the volume in the KIND_VOLUME
//                              table. Fires from probe_one_bdev's
//                              LIVE-arm success emit, reached via
//                              kernel_main's `call pdxb_volume_probe_
//                              all_bdev` (#1743).
//   (2) PDXFS BOOT MOUNT OK    pdxfs_boot_mount_smoke_witness (#1722)
//                              exercises mount_pdxfs_block against the
//                              LIVE volume (backend=5, MOUNT_FLAG_VALID
//                              set at slot 0) and emits its OK line
//                              after every stage of the six-check LIVE
//                              arm passes (see that witness's header).
//   (3) PDXB VOLUME MOUNTED    mount_pdxfs_block (#1707) emits this
//                              once the mount_table entry is packed and
//                              the KIND_VOLUME cap has been minted --
//                              R53.M3-005 fingerprint hook.
//   (4) PDXB ROOT SELECTED     root_select's (#1744) LIVE arm fires
//                              from pdxb_root_select_fingerprint_call
//                              once the registry has a single live
//                              volume the single-device disambiguation
//                              picks.
//   (5) FIRST MOUNT OK         THIS witness -- terminal ordered line
//                              closing the sequence.
//
// The five-line golden is checked with the smoke runner's ordered-
// substring semantic (tools/run-smoke.sh:1265+): each line must appear
// in the serial log in the order listed, and a missing prior line fails
// the check at THAT line, not here. This closing line therefore has one
// job: mark the terminal ordered position past which no further R53.M4
// fingerprint is expected.
//
// =============================================================================
// WHY UNCONDITIONAL EMIT (NOT A GATED "IF ALL PRIOR STAGES OK" CHECK)
// =============================================================================
//
// The ordered-subsequence golden already enforces precedence over the
// four upstream fingerprints. A gated closer that scanned the klog ring
// for each prior fingerprint would (a) duplicate the check inside the
// kernel with weaker semantics (ring history is bounded; the smoke
// check reads the whole serial log), (b) require a witness-only "did I
// see line X?" primitive no other module needs, and (c) create a second
// failure mode that reports "SEQUENCE INCOMPLETE" when the real cause
// is one of four upstream witnesses -- the diagnostic would point at
// the wrong place. This posture mirrors pdxfs_round_trip_final.pdx's
// own "unconditional emit, defer the gating to the ordered-subsequence
// golden" argument one-for-one; the two witnesses close two different
// PdxFS smoke sequences with the same closer shape.
//
// A substrate-mode boot (no --with-disk, every default smoke matrix
// run) still emits this line -- the fingerprint has no branch on
// _mount_table state. That is safe by construction: the R53.M4-003
// mode dispatcher gates on WITH_DISK=1 and exits 2 without it, so the
// four LIVE-arm fingerprints (PDXB PROBE OK / PDXFS BOOT MOUNT OK /
// PDXB VOLUME MOUNTED / PDXB ROOT SELECTED) can only appear when the
// LIVE arm was reachable, and the ordered check on the golden binds
// FIRST MOUNT OK to the tail of that specific sequence. Existing
// substrate-mode goldens (tests/r17/shell-shutdown.golden and its
// siblings) use the same ordered-substring matcher, so an additional
// unpinned line between "PDXB ROOT FALLBACK" and "ROUND TRIP OK" adds
// no golden churn (a golden pins what MUST appear, not what MAY
// appear).
//
// =============================================================================
// FINGERPRINT CONTRACT
// =============================================================================
//
// "FIRST MOUNT OK\n"
//
// Output-strip-clean per design/policy/output-provenance-strip.md and
// the sibling R53 witness convention: no round tag, no milestone tag,
// no issue tag. The golden pins the exact byte sequence; a regression
// that shortens/lengthens the emit would fail the golden at this line.
// The fingerprint is asserted in tests/r53/first-mount.golden line 5
// (the only golden that asserts it), which satisfies the R49.M3/#1578
// fingerprint-coverage gate.
//
// =============================================================================
// STACK / EFFECT / CAPABILITY POSTURE
// =============================================================================
//
// Caller (r30_platform.pdx's boot_continue_after_ring3 body) invokes
// via `call pdxfs_first_mount_witness` with rsp%16 == 8 (the same
// parity every other closer in that function's tail relies on -- see
// r30_platform.pdx's own file header on the single-`push rbp` inline
// parity restoration this module inherits). One `push rbp` at entry
// lands rsp%16 == 0 for the klog_s1 call. No callee-save preservation
// otherwise needed: klog_s1 preserves all SysV callee-saves per its
// own contract, and this body touches no other callee-save register.
//
// Effect row {sysreg, mem} matches klog_s1's own row exactly (sysreg
// for the underlying uart_putc it drives + mem for the ring append).
// Capability row {boot} matches the caller's row: this witness runs
// only during boot_continue_after_ring3, and gains no authority beyond
// what the caller already holds.
//
// Return value: always 0 (OK). Not consumed by the caller today, but
// matches the sibling closer witnesses' (u64 -> u64) shape so any
// future gated variant can return 1 on assertion failure without
// changing the signature.
//
// =============================================================================
// LABEL RESERVATION
// =============================================================================
//
// All local labels prefixed `pfm_` (per reserved-label discipline; the
// pdxfs_first_mount subsystem is unclaimed elsewhere -- grep audit
// 2026-08-23: no `pfm_` hits anywhere else in src/kernel/). Reserved so
// that a future gated variant's body labels can use the same prefix
// without collision with any sibling witness.

module PdxfsFirstMount = structure {

  // Fingerprint bytes. 14 chars + newline + NUL = 16 bytes.
  pub let pfm_ok_msg : [u8; 16] = "FIRST MOUNT OK\n\0"

  // ==========================================================================
  // pdxfs_first_mount_witness() -> 0 (OK)
  //
  // Emits "FIRST MOUNT OK\n" as the terminal line of the R53.M4 first-
  // mount smoke fingerprint sequence. Registered after
  // pdxb_root_select_fingerprint_call and before pdxfs_round_trip_
  // final_call in src/kernel/boot/witness/r30_platform.pdx so the
  // ordered-subsequence golden pin (tests/r53/first-mount.golden) is
  // well-defined.
  // ==========================================================================
  pub let pdxfs_first_mount_witness : () -> u64 !{sysreg, mem} @{boot} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {sysreg, mem}, capabilities: {boot},
      justification: "R53.M4-003 (#1750) terminal closer witness for the boot_r53_first_mount smoke. Emits one output-strip-clean fingerprint (FIRST MOUNT OK) as the terminal ordered line the tests/r53/first-mount.golden pins. Unconditional emit rather than gated closer: the ordered-subsequence smoke check already enforces precedence over the four upstream fingerprints (PDXB PROBE OK from probe.pdx, PDXFS BOOT MOUNT OK from pdxfs_boot_mount_smoke.pdx, PDXB VOLUME MOUNTED from mount_block.pdx, PDXB ROOT SELECTED from root_select.pdx), so any missing prior stage fails at THAT line rather than as a false-positive here (see file header's diagnostic-locality argument, mirroring pdxfs_round_trip_final.pdx's identical closer shape). Single `push rbp` lands rsp%16 == 0 for the klog_s1 call (entry parity is rsp%16 == 8 per r30_platform's own alignment inherited from boot_continue_after_ring3 -- see r30_platform.pdx file header). No callee-save preservation beyond rbp: klog_s1 preserves all SysV callee-saves per its own contract, and this body touches no other callee-save register. Effect {sysreg,mem} matches klog_s1's own row (sysreg for underlying uart_putc + mem for ring append); capability {boot} matches r30_platform_run's caller row. Labels prefixed pfm_.",
      block: {
        push rbp;

        mov rdi, 3;                          // klog level INFO
        lea rsi, [rip + SUBSYS_BOOT];
        lea rdx, [rip + pfm_ok_msg];
        call klog_s1;

        xor rax, rax;
        pop rbp;
        ret
      }
    }
}
